implementationPlan.description:
VERIFY, once, after step 1. The shared checkout's packages/moe-daemon/node_modules is win32, and Linux vitest can't load rolldown from it, so run both legs in snapshots.

Linux:
- Follow mem:gotcha-daemon-linux-snapshot-gate and mem:gotcha-linux-vitest-reuse-native-node-modules:
  - git archive HEAD of the whole repo;
  - overlay ONLY packages/moe-daemon/src/index.test.ts and cmp it against the worktree;
  - link a Linux node_modules whose package-lock matches;
  - run under env -i, so MOE_* is unset, with NO_COLOR=1.
- Run exactly `cd packages/moe-daemon && npm test` (the full daemon package suite, about 20s). Its exitCode and outputTail are the complete_task verification.

Native Windows:
- Use the same single-file overlay in a Windows temp snapshot (mem:gotcha-gate-hermetic-snapshot-from-wsl, mem:gotcha-windows-fixture-cwd-cleanup).
- Run `cd packages/moe-daemon && npx vitest run src/index.test.ts`. X15 must RUN, not skip, with the drive-less /x alias. Cite the counts and the log path.

If anything unrelated fails:
- reproduce it at the same HEAD without the overlay;
- file a bug row;
- cite both runs, and don't fix it here.

Delete only your own mktemp dirs, guarded by exact path.

ADVERSARIAL SELF-REVIEW, once, as the final step. Load adversarial-self-review. Check:
- Isolation: no lock survives between writers. A failing assertion still restores the cwd (afterEach), and the outer afterEach removes testDir. Nothing depends on X14's child or on test order.
- Spellings:
  - DEAD_PID is ESRCH on both OSes (the existing 'DEAD_PID is not a live pid here' row);
  - the Windows alias needs the cwd on testDir's drive (the fixture asserts this);
  - dotted and trailing-separator forms;
  - 8.3 short tmp names.
- Expectations are exact strings and tuples, never toBeFalsy or toBeTruthy.
- Diff: only index.test.ts, about 40 net lines or fewer:
  - the import plus X15;
  - no index.ts or runtime change;
  - no new skip or todo;
  - X1-X14 untouched.
Fix any finding and rerun the step-2 gate.

Then call complete_task with:
- the Linux verification;
- the Windows counts;
- both mutant results;
- one line per DoD item:
  - DoD1: the fix landed in 25ba449a, and X15 asserts it for raw //x (Linux), /x (native Windows), relative and dotted spellings;
  - DoD2: temp testDir only, never the live .moe.
Name the residual non-goals: symlinks/junctions, 8.3 short names, \\?\ prefixes, and case-insensitive macOS volumes. path.resolve never folded these, so they are pre-existing and not this row.
